WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Peter Thiel is one of the most&nbsp;
legendary investors in Silicon Valley.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.440
“I build companies and I support people&nbsp;
who are building new things. From social&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.880
networks to rocket ships” He’s helped build&nbsp;
PayPal, Facebook, and Palantir into massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.920
multi-billion dollar companies. And now he has&nbsp;
his sights set on space manufacturing. And I’m&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.800
not talking about making rockets here on earth,&nbsp;
when I say “Space Manufacturing” I actually mean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.440
producing physical goods in low earth orbit,&nbsp;
and then bringing them back down to earth.
&nbsp;

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.800
If that all sounds a little crazy, don’t&nbsp;
worry, it was completely new to me when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.240
I started working on this video. But I’m going&nbsp;
to take you through the fascinating history of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:40.080
space manufacturing and then work through exactly&nbsp;
how Thiel is planning to make this a reality.
&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.920
When you’re a multi-billionaire like Thiel, you&nbsp;
don’t need to get your hands dirty with founding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.680
a company to attack an interesting problem&nbsp;
any more. Thiel has created a platform for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.600
building and scaling the most promising&nbsp;
business ideas with Founders Fund, his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.960
$6 billion dollar investment firm. And Founders&nbsp;
Fund isn’t like most venture capital shops.
&nbsp;

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.680
The majority of VCs focus on meeting&nbsp;
entrepreneurs that are running existing businesses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.000
and then giving them money to help grow what’s&nbsp;
already working. They usually take a board seat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.680
and help set the high level strategy, but&nbsp;
it doesn’t go much deeper than that. 
&nbsp;

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.320
And Founders Fund does do a lot of deals&nbsp;
that look exactly like that. But recently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:19.360
they’ve been going a level deeper and actually&nbsp;
co-founding companies alongside entrepreneurs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.280
They did this with the defense technology&nbsp;
company Anduril, where Trae Stephens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.160
who’s a partner at Founders Fund, stepped up to&nbsp;
co-found the company alongside Palmer Luckey.
&nbsp;

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:33.440
This model is typically called “an incubation”&nbsp;
or “a venture studio company” and there have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:37.680
been some massive successes. The cloud&nbsp;
data storage company Snowflake was started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.560
this way by Sutter Hill Ventures and is&nbsp;
now worth $80 billion dollars. And this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.200
is the model that Thiel and Founders Fund are&nbsp;
using to make space manufacturing a reality.
&nbsp;

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.600
At the center of this project is Delian&nbsp;
Asparouhov, he’s a VC at Founders Fund and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.960
a cofounder of Varda Space Industries. He’d been&nbsp;
tracking the trends in the aerospace industry for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:02.240
years and assembled a team to help build this new&nbsp;
company. The name Varda is a Tolkein reference,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:06.000
like the other Founders Fund&nbsp;
incubations, Palantir and Anduril. 
&nbsp;

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.240
Delian has basically been speedrunning&nbsp;
Silicon Valley for the past 8 years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:14.960
His resume has it all. TED Talk. Check. MIT&nbsp;
Dropout. Check. Startup Founder. Check. Y&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:20.480
Combinator. Check. Startup Investor. Check.
And now he’s basically speedrunning the company&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:25.440
building process. Varda raised a $9 million&nbsp;
dollar seed round back in December of 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:31.280
and they just closed a $42 million dollar Series&nbsp;
A in July of 2021. That’s a pretty insane amount&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.400
of money to raise so quickly, but Delian has a&nbsp;
unique strategy for capturing this new market&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.680
that completely justifies a more&nbsp;
aggressive fundraising timeline.
&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.840
The typical path in Silicon Valley used&nbsp;
to be: work at a big company for 10 years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:49.120
then work on a startup for the next ten, and&nbsp;
then become a VC in your forties. But Delian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:54.160
is moving ridiculously quickly, which will be&nbsp;
a big theme throughout this story. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.160 --> 00:03:00.160
he is so obsessed with speed that he counts the&nbsp;
